<article class="env-lemma" id="01K1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01K1">Lemma <span data-tag="01K1">26.18.5</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Consider the diagrams </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \vcenter { \xymatrix{ X_ s \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\kappa (s)) \ar[r] &  S } } \quad \text{and}\quad \vcenter { \xymatrix{ \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, s}) \times _ S X \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X \ar[d] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\mathcal{O}_{S, s}) \ar[r] &  S } }  \]
</div>
  <p> In both cases these diagrams induce fibre squares of topological spaces and in particular, the top horizontal arrow is a homeomorphism onto its image. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose an open affine $U \subset S$ that contains $s$. The bottom horizontal morphisms factor through $U$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/01J6" data-tag="01J6">26.13.1</a> for example. Thus we may assume that $S$ is affine. If $X$ is also affine, then the result follows from Algebra, Remark <a href="/tag/00E6" data-tag="00E6">10.18.5</a>. In the general case the result follows by covering $X$ by open affines. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>